---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { LINKEDIN_URL, SCHEDULING_LINK } from '../consts';

const influences = [
	{
		name: 'Shape Up',
		href: 'https://basecamp.com/shapeup',
		note: 'from Basecamp. Fixed time, variable scope. It’s why the budget is fixed and the scope moves.',
	},
	{
		name: 'The Lean Startup',
		href: 'https://theleanstartup.com/',
		note: 'by Eric Ries. The experiment as the unit of work.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Incorruptible',
		href: 'https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Incorruptible/Eric-Ries/9798893311860',
		note: 'Eric Ries again. Build things that create more value than they take.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Design thinking',
		href: 'https://designthinking.ideo.com/',
		note: 'as IDEO teaches it. Put the thing in real hands before you trust your own opinion of it.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Pivotal Labs',
		href: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pivotal_Labs',
		note: 'where a team learns all of this by doing it next to someone for a few months.',
	},
];
---

<MarketingLayout
	title="Work | People Purpose Product"
	description="Fractional product ownership and product owner coaching for mission-driven teams, and what a typical month looks like."
>
	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure page-header">
			<h1>Work</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Funded teams with a real problem come to me with one of two gaps: nobody in the
				product owner seat, or someone in it who's never been shown the craft. Here's what I
				do about each, and how to tell if it fits.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap services">
		<div class="label ruled">How we work together</div>

		<article class="service">
			<h2>Fractional product owner</h2>
			<p>
				The roadmap stays yours. I take the product owner seat on your team and sit in the
				meetings: drafting the requirements, designing the experiments, reading what comes
				back, making the call with your people in the room.
			</p>
			<p>
				A product manager who runs the product day to day is table stakes. The part that's
				harder to find is ownership: deciding what gets built, in what order, and standing
				behind the call. I do both.
			</p>
			<div class="fit-strip">
				<div class="fit yes">
					<span class="fit-k">Fits when</span>
					<span class="fit-v">You already have engineers, and nobody deciding what they build.</span>
				</div>
				<div class="fit">
					<span class="fit-k">Does not fit when</span>
					<span class="fit-v">You have a mature backlog and want a technical product manager to run it. That's a different hire, and I'll say so on the call.</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</article>

		<article class="service">
			<h2>Product owner coaching</h2>
			<p>
				For the person already doing this job without the title. We draft the roadmap
				together, run the experiments together, and sit in it together when an idea
				flops. Then you keep doing it after I'm gone.
			</p>
			<div class="fit-strip">
				<div class="fit yes">
					<span class="fit-k">Fits when</span>
					<span class="fit-v">Someone on your team has the instincts and has never had anyone to learn the craft from.</span>
				</div>
				<div class="fit">
					<span class="fit-k">Does not fit when</span>
					<span class="fit-v">Nobody on the team has time in the seat. The coaching is the doing, so the person needs hours, not just interest.</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</article>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure month">
			<h2>What a typical month looks like</h2>
			<p>
				I can do it for you. I can teach you how. What works best is doing it with you.
			</p>
			<div class="once">
				<span class="once-k">Before the first month</span>
				<span>A 30-minute call</span>
				<span>I sit in on one or two of your meetings</span>
				<span>We prioritize the risks and assumptions, and draft a roadmap if the project needs one</span>
			</div>
			<div class="month-cols">
				<div class="col every">
					<div class="col-k">Every week</div>
					<ol class="week-steps">
						<li>We read what came back and make the call: keep it, change it, or drop it.</li>
						<li>We write the next build, and the experiment that tells us whether it helped.</li>
						<li>We build the smallest thing that tests it: a prototype, a form, or a feature.</li>
						<li>It goes in real hands.</li>
					</ol>
				</div>
				<div class="col">
					<div class="col-k">End of the month</div>
					<ul class="month-end">
						<li>A readout: what we saw, and what we do next.</li>
						<li>Engagements run month to month. We size next month's work to your budget. The scope moves. The invoice does not.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p>
				Every engagement ends the same way. Your team runs the month without me.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure influences">
			<h2>Where this comes from</h2>
			<p>My school of product ownership had many teachers. A few I keep going back to:</p>
			<ul>
				{influences.map((i) => (
					<li><a href={i.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{i.name}</a>, {i.note}</li>
				))}
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure closing">
			<h2>Let's talk</h2>
			<p>
				If any of this resonates, I'd love to talk. Book 30 minutes and tell me what
				you're working on.
			</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="primary" href={SCHEDULING_LINK} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find a time &rarr;</a>
				<span class="aside">Prefer email? Write me at <a class="email-link" href={LINKEDIN_URL}>hello at this domain</a>.</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</MarketingLayout>

<script>
	// Assemble the address in the browser so scrapers reading the raw HTML
	// never see a complete email. The href above is a fallback (LinkedIn)
	// for the rare no-JS visitor.
	const user = 'hello';
	const domain = 'peoplepurposeproduct.com';
	const address = `${user}@${domain}`;
	document.querySelectorAll('.email-link').forEach((el) => {
		el.setAttribute('href', `mailto:${address}`);
		el.textContent = address;
	});
</script>

<style>
	.page-header {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 24px;
		padding: 96px 0 56px;
	}
	.lede {
		font-size: 22px;
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: var(--body);
	}

	.services {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		padding-bottom: 32px;
	}
	/* Each service runs the full width: heading, body at the page measure,
	   then a two-cell strip. The green rule marks the "fits" cell. */
	.service {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 16px;
		padding: 30px 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-light);
	}
	.service h2 {
		font-size: 26px;
		line-height: 1.2;
	}
	.service p {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		font-size: 18px;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--body);
	}
	.fit-strip {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 32px;
		margin-top: 6px;
	}
	.fit {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 4px;
		padding-top: 12px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}
	.fit.yes {
		border-top-color: var(--link);
	}
	.fit-k {
		font-size: 12px;
		line-height: 1.4;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.fit-v {
		font-size: 16px;
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: var(--body-soft);
	}

	.month,
	.influences {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 18px;
		padding: 32px 0 56px;
	}
	.month p,
	.influences p,
	.closing p {
		font-size: 19px;
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--body);
	}
	/* The month: a "once" line, then every week beside the end of the month. */
	.once {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 6px 28px;
		align-items: baseline;
		padding: 14px 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-light);
		font-size: 16px;
		color: var(--body-soft);
	}
	.once-k,
	.col-k {
		font-size: 12px;
		line-height: 1.4;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.once-k {
		flex-basis: 100%;
	}
	.once span:not(.once-k)::before {
		content: '○  ';
		font-size: 10px;
		vertical-align: 2px;
		color: var(--company);
	}
	.month-cols {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 3fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
		gap: 40px;
	}
	.col {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 12px;
		padding-top: 12px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}
	.col.every {
		border-top-color: var(--link);
	}
	.week-steps,
	.month-end {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 10px;
		font-size: 18px;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--body);
	}
	.week-steps {
		counter-reset: step;
	}
	.week-steps li {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 2.2em minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 8px;
		counter-increment: step;
	}
	.week-steps li::before {
		content: counter(step) '.';
		color: var(--muted);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}
	.lists {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 40px;
		padding-top: 8px;
	}
	.list {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 10px;
	}
	.list h3 {
		font-size: 20px;
	}
	.list ul,
	.influences ul {
		padding-left: 1.2em;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 8px;
		font-size: 17px;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--body-soft);
	}
	.influences ul {
		font-size: 19px;
		color: var(--body);
	}
	.influences {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
		padding-top: 48px;
	}

	.closing {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 18px;
		padding: 48px 0 72px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.page-header {
			padding: 48px 0 40px;
			gap: 18px;
		}
		.lede {
			font-size: 20px;
		}
		.service {
			gap: 14px;
			padding: 24px 0;
		}
		.service h2 {
			font-size: 24px;
		}
		.fit-strip {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 14px;
		}
		.month,
		.influences {
			padding: 24px 0 48px;
		}
		.lists {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 24px;
		}
		.once {
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 6px;
		}
		.month-cols {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 24px;
		}
		.closing {
			padding: 40px 0 56px;
		}
	}
</style>
